QuestGuidance.Register("en",62,{
[1953]="7000D4C2\n1\tTalk to Gwathryn\tGwathryn is at Tármunn Súrsa, east of Carn Dûm, in Angmar. Elrond bade you return to Gwathryn and seek out the location of Narchuil, the ring of Amarthiel.\n",
[1954]="7000D558\n1\tCollect Watching Stone Orders\tBarad Dúrgul is west of Tármunn Súrsa. Gwathryn has sent you to defeat the Gate-wards of the Angmarim and learn what you may about the silent watching-stones.\n2\tTalk to Gwathryn\030Collect Watching Stone Orders\tGwathryn is at Tármunn Súrsa, east of Barad Dúrgul. You should bring the watching-stone orders to Gwathryn.\n",
[1955]="70037972\n1\tTravel to the entrance of Woodhurst, in the Stonedeans\tWoodhurst is located in the northern stretches of the Stonedeans, west of the Broadacres.\n2\tTalk to Nona by the entrance to Woodhurst\030Talk to Horn by the entrance to Woodhurst\tNona and Horn are at the northern entrance to Woodhurst, in the Stonedeans.\n3\tTalk to Briant in the hideout on the outskirts of Woodhurst\tBriant is inside her son's hideout, in Woodhurst. You do not know where Reeve Heremond is. The hideout is on the outskirts of Woodhurst. You should find Reeve Heremond or his wife Briant in Woodhurst, and convey the message from Reeve Fríthild that Woodhurst may be in danger.\n4\tTalk to Herubrand in the hideout on the outskirts of Woodhurst\tHerubrand is in the hideout on the outskirts of Woodhurst. Briant has told you to speak with her son Herubrand about the situation in Woodhurst.\n5\tDefeat Dunlending invaders throughout the Stonedeans (total: 10)\tDunlending invaders can be found throughout the Stonedeans, especially in Woodhurst.\n6\tTalk to Herubrand in the hideout on the outskirts of Woodhurst\tHerubrand is in the hideout on the outskirts of Woodhurst. You have defeated many Dunlending invaders and should report of your success to Herubrand.\n",
[1956]="70037977\n1\tTalk to Horn at the entrance to Woodhurst\tHorn is at the entrance to Woodhurst. Heruband has offered to bring you before the soothsayer Hildegard, but first you should see what Horn and Nona think of the prospect.\n2\tTalk to Nona at the entrance to Woodhurst\tNona is at the entrance to Woodhurst. Heruband has offered to bring you before the soothsayer Hildegard, but first you should see what Horn and Nona think of the prospect.\n3\tTalk to Herubrand and go with him to meet the soothsayer\tHerubrand is in the cellar of his hideout, on the outskirts of Woodhurst. Horn and Nona have agreed to meet with the soothsayer, with varying degrees of excitement, and now you should tell Herubrand you are ready to go.\n4\tTalk to Nona by the entrance to Woodhurst\030Talk to Horn by the entrance to Woodhurst\tHorn and Nona are at the entrance to Woodhurst, in the Stonedeans. You have had a curious encounter with the soothsayer, Hildegard, and should now speak of the experience with your companions.\n5\tTalk to Herubrand in his hideout, in Woodhurst\tHerubrand is in the cellar of his hideout, on the outskirts of Woodhurst. You have returned from meeting the soothsayer Hildegard, and should report now to Herubrand.\n",
[1957]="7000D4C3\n1\tRecover Narchuil\tGwathryn is at Tármunn Súrsa in Angmar. Gwathryn has bid you enter Barad Dúrgul and recover the ring Narchuil. Narucham awaits you within the fortress. This quest is meant for a fellowship. If you choose to undertake this quest solo you will receive an inspiration bonus, but the challenge will be great.\n2\tTalk to Gwathryn\030Collect Half of the Ring Narchuil\tGwathryn is at Tármunn Súrsa in Angmar. You should report at once to Gwathryn.\n",
[1958]="7000E05B\n1\tBring the ring-fragment to Elrond in Rivendell\tElrond is in the library on the top floor of the Last Homely House in Rivendell, in the Trollshaws. Arvedui confirmed that the ring-fragment was the lost half of Narchuil and bid you take it to Elrond in Rivendell.\n2\tTalk to Aragorn in Rivendell\tAragorn is in one of the guest rooms of Elrond's House. Elrond bade you speak to Aragorn of your meeting with the shade of Arvedui, his ancestor.\n",
[1959]="700379F3\n1\tIn the hours before dawn, the forces of Saruman press their advantage. There are two ways to participate in the defence of the Hornburg. You can speak to Cenric for the Storied Tale, a story-focused experience. Or you can use the Epic Battles Panel for a more gameplay-intensive experience. To participate in the defence of the Hornburg, open the Epic Battles Panel and select 'The Hornburg' from the menu. After you successfully complete the defence, you will be returned to the location from which you entered it.\t\n2\tTalk to Gléowine by the map table near the western wall of the Hornburg\tIn the hours before dawn, the forces of Saruman press their advantage. Gléowine is on the first level, west of the Hornburg.\n3\tPick up the banner leaning against the western wall, and time will pass\tDay has dawned, and with it comes new hope for Rohan. Gléowine has hurried off to hear what has happened, but Thurketel is nearby and his face speaks volumes.\n4\tTalk to Thurketel\tDay has dawned, and with it comes new hope for Rohan. Thurketel is by the map table west of the Hornburg.\n",
[1960]="700379F6\n1\tFind Aragorn and Théoden on the field outside the gates\tDay has dawned, and with it comes new hope for Rohan. Thurketel has asked you to go out the front gate, and see what has become of the battle.\n2\tTalk to Aragorn on the field of victory\030Talk to Théoden on the field of victory\tDay has dawned, and with it comes new hope for Rohan. Aragorn and Théoden are outside the walls of the Deep, on the field of victory.\n3\tTalk to Gandalf on the field of victory\tDay has dawned, and with it comes new hope for Rohan. Gandalf has arrived at Helm's Deep. What part did he play in the victory?\n4\tTalk to Éomer on the field of victory\tDay has dawned, and with it comes new hope for Rohan. Éomer is overseeing the surrender of many Dunlendings following the battle.\n5\tTalk to the frightened Dunlending warrior by Éomer\tDay has dawned, and with it comes new hope for Rohan. Éomer is on the field of battle, trying to accept the surrender of some surviving Dunlending warriors.\n6\tTalk to Legolas on the field of victory\030Talk to Gimli on the field of victory\tDay has dawned, and with it comes new hope for Rohan. Legolas and Gimli are somewhere on the field of victory.\n7\tTalk to Gandalf on the field of victory\tDay has dawned, and with it comes new hope for Rohan. Gandalf is on the field of victory before the walls of Helm's Deep.\n",
[1961]="7000E05C\n1\tTalk to Laerdan\tLaerdan is in his chambers in the Last Homely House. Aragorn bade you seek out Laerdan and tell him of your search for Narchuil.\n",
[1962]="700379A3\n1\tFollow the road that runs from Helm's Dike to the Hornburg\030Talk to Gimli at Helm's Dike\030Talk to Thurketel along the road from the Dike\tA road runs from Helm's Dike through the valley and to the Hornburg.\n2\tFind the guard-house of the Hornburg\030Talk to Háma at the guard-house of the Hornburg\030Talk to Déorwine at the guard-house of the Hornburg\tThe guard-house provides a sturdy defence for the Hornburg.\n3\tFind Legolas atop the Deeping Wall\030Talk to Legolas atop the wall\030Talk to Sigferth atop the wall\tThe Deeping Wall provides a sturdy defence for the Hornburg, and allows its defenders a commanding view of the gorge.\n4\tFind Théoden and Éomer outside the keep of the Hornburg\030Talk to Théoden outside the keep of the Hornburg\030Talk to Éomer outside the keep of the Hornburg\tThéoden and Éomer are overseeing the preparations outside the Hornburg.\n5\tTalk to Aragorn outside the keep of the Hornburg\tAragorn is outside the keep of the Hornburg, alongside Éomer and not far from Théoden.\n",
[1963]="7000E05A\n1\tTalk to Laerdan\tLaerdan is in his quarters on the first floor of the Last Homely House. Elrond has asked you to speak with Laerdan and learn what course of action he intends to take.\n",
[1964]="70016AA0\n1\tTalk to Laerdan\tLaerdan is in his quarters on the first floor of the Last Homely House. Elrond has asked you to speak with Laerdan and learn what course of action he intends to take.\n",
[1965]="700379A6\n1\tRetrieve iron goods from a barrel near Aragorn, outside the keep of the Hornburg\tBarrels of iron goods from the farmers of Westfold can be found outside the keep of the Hornburg, near Aragorn. Aragorn has asked you to sort through an iron goods barrel using one of the nearby sorting mats.\n2\tUse the mat near Aragorn to sort through the iron goods\tYou can use one of the mats near Aragorn to sort the iron goods contributed by the farmers of Westfold.\n3\tUse the mat near Aragorn to sort through the iron goods\tYou can use one of the mats near Aragorn to sort the iron goods contributed by the farmers of Westfold.\n4\tUse the mat near Aragorn to sort through the iron goods\tYou can use one of the mats near Aragorn to sort the iron goods contributed by the farmers of Westfold.\n5\tTalk to Éomer outside the keep of the Hornburg\tÉomer is outside the keep of the Hornburg.\n6\tPick up one of the training dummies near Éomer\tÉomer has asked you to carry one of the nearby training dummies up to the wall by Legolas, the better to draw fire away from the defenders.\n7\tTalk to Legolas atop the wall\tLegolas is atop the wall. You have carried a training dummy to the top of the wall and Legolas has caught your eye.\n8\tTalk to Corudan by his horse at Helm's Dike\tCorudan has gone down to the Dike, beyond the walls of the Hornburg. Legolas told you that Corudan planned to scout the armies of Saruman, and you should speak to him before he leaves.\n9\tTalk to Gamling at Helm's Dike\tGamling is at Helm's Dike. There is always work to be done to get ready for battle, and Gamling will tell you what he needs.\n10\tPick up the barrel of iron goods near Gamling, in Helm's Dike\tGamling has asked you to carry a barrel of iron goods from Helm's Dike to Aragorn outside the keep of the Hornburg.\n11\tTalk to Aragorn outside the keep of the Hornburg\tAragorn is outside the keep of the Hornburg, and wishes to speak with you.\n",
[1966]="7000E05D\n1\tTalk to Dáthi\tDáthi is at Kauppa-kohta in the land of Forochel north of Evendim through the Gate to the North. Laerdan has asked you to go to Forochel and speak with the dwarf-trader Dáthi. it may be that the dwarf will know where to begin the search for Narchuil.\n2\tTalk to Lassi\tLassi is at Sûri-kylä north and east along the Ice Bay of Forochel. Dáthi told you of Laerdan's last visit and of the arrival of the Angmarim. He told you to speak with Lassi if you hope to recover Narchuil before the Angmarim.\n",
[1967]="7000E060\n1\tTalk to Sini\tSini is on the outskirts of Sûri-kylä. Lassi instructed you to speak with Sini about tasks with which to gain the favour of Yrjänä.\n2\tFind Urmas\tUrmas was last seen heading south towards Itä-mâ. Sini has instructed you to go into the wild to find Urmas.\n3\tTalk to Sini\tSini is on the outskirts of Sûri-kylä. You have found Urmas and should now return to Sini to report your success.\n",
[1968]="7000E05F\n1\tTalk to Emeli\tEmeli is near the entrance to Sûri-kylä. You should seek out Emeli if you wish to gain the favour of strength.\n2\tCollect Paksu-karva's tusk\tPaksu-karva was last seen among worms south-east along the Ice Bay. Emeli instructed you to seek Paksu-karva and bring him its tusk as a sign that you have completed the feat of strength required of you.\n3\tTalk to Emeli\030Collect Snow-worm Tusk\tEmeli is at Sûri-kylä across from the steam-lodge. You should return the tusk of Paksu-karva to Emeli as a sign of your success.\n",
[1969]="7000E061\n1\tTalk to Jalmari\tJalmari is at Sûri-kylä near to the steam-lodge. Lassi has instructed you to speak with Jalmari and receive from him guidance to help earn the favour of Yrjänä.\n2\tChoose the first item\tThe items can be found next to Jalmari. Jalmari has instructed you to use wisdom in ordering certain items of import to the Lossoth. he told you the following in regard to the items: 'Warmth is of great importance in these frozen lands, so fire is a boon companion. Even more important is water, for without water there is no life. 'Even with fire and water at your disposal, these lands are not safe. A wise person will take with him stout weapons to protect himself, though he must first have food enough to lend himself the strength to wield such weapons. 'Above all, a wanderer in these lands must have clothing warm enough to protect him against the cold when fire cannot be made.' This stage includes failure conditions; check the journal before choosing objects or actions.\n3\tChoose the second item\tThe items can be found next to Jalmari in Sûri-kylä. Jalmari has instructed you to use wisdom in ordering certain items of import to the Lossoth. he told you the following in regard to the items: 'Warmth is of great importance in these frozen lands, so fire is a boon companion. Even more important is water, for without water there is no life. 'Even with fire and water at your disposal, these lands are not safe. A wise person will take with him stout weapons to protect himself, though he must first have food enough to lend himself the strength to wield such weapons. 'Above all, a wanderer in these lands must have clothing warm enough to protect him against the cold when fire cannot be made.' This stage includes failure conditions; check the journal before choosing objects or actions.\n4\tChoose the third item\tThe items can be found next to Jalmari in Sûri-kylä. Jalmari has instructed you to use wisdom in ordering certain items off import to the Lossoth. He told you the following in regard to the items: 'Warmth is of great importance in these frozen lands, so fire is a boon companion. Even more important is water, for without water there is no life. 'Even with fire and water at your disposal, these lands are not safe. A wise person will take with him stout weapons to protect himself, though he must first have food enough to lend himself the strength to wield such weapons. 'Above all, a wanderer in these lands must have clothing warm enough to protect him against the cold when fire cannot be made.' This stage includes failure conditions; check the journal before choosing objects or actions.\n5\tChoose the fourth item\tThe items can be found next to Jalmari in Sûri-kylä. Jalmari has instructed you to use wisdom in ordering certain items off import to the Lossoth. He told you the following in regard to the items: 'Warmth is of great importance in these frozen lands, so fire is a boon companion. Even more important is water, for without water there is no life. 'Even with fire and water at your disposal, these lands are not safe. A wise person will take with him stout weapons to protect himself, though he must first have food enough to lend himself the strength to wield such weapons. 'Above all, a wanderer in these lands must have clothing warm enough to protect him against the cold when fire cannot be made.' This stage includes failure conditions; check the journal before choosing objects or actions.\n6\tChoose the fifth item\tThe items can be found next to Jalmari in Sûri-kylä. Jalmari has instructed you to use wisdom in ordering certain items off import to the Lossoth. He told you the following in regard to the items: 'Warmth is of great importance in these frozen lands, so fire is a boon companion. Even more important is water, for without water there is no life. 'Even with fire and water at your disposal, these lands are not safe. A wise person will take with him stout weapons to protect himself, though he must first have food enough to lend himself the strength to wield such weapons. 'Above all, a wanderer in these lands must have clothing warm enough to protect him against the cold when fire cannot be made.' This stage includes failure conditions; check the journal before choosing objects or actions.\n7\tTalk to Jalmari\tJalmari is at Sûri-kylä near to the steam-lodge. You should return to Jalmari with the solution to his puzzle.\n",
[1970]="7000E05E\n1\tAcquire the Favour of Strength\030Acquire the Favour of Endurance\030Acquire the Favour of Wisdom\tJalmari stands inside Sûri-kylä near to the steam-lodge. Emeli stands across from the steam-lodge. Sini stands on the outskirts of Sûri-kylä. Lassi has told you that three tasks must be completed before you may speak with Yrjänä. You should speak with him again if you wish to learn more.\n2\tTalk to Yrjänä\tYrjänä is at the Great Lodge in Sûri-kylä. Now that you have completed the tasks required of you, you should speak with Yrjänä.\n",
[1971]="700379A9\n1\tTalk to Gléowine near the map table by the western wall\tGléowine is on the lowest level of the fortress, by a pile of straw near the west wall. Aragorn wants to determine the mood of Théoden, but has sent you not to the King but to Gléowine to learn it.\n2\tStudy the map table near the western wall, by Gléowine, and time will pass\tGléowine wants you to show him on the nearby map table what the night may hold for the defenders of Helm's Deep. Interacting with the map table near Gléowine will allow time to pass. Action will resume after midnight, when the battle is joined.\n3\tTalk to Gléowine, by the map table near the western wall, after midnight\tIt is after midnight at Helm's Deep. Gléowine is by the map table, near the pile of straw by the western wall.\n4\tTalk to Gamling by the pile of straw near the western wall\tIt is after midnight at Helm's Deep. Gamling is by the map table with Gléowine, on the lowest level of the fortress, by the western wall.\n",
[1972]="700379AB\n1\tGamling has asked for your help defending Helm's Dike. There are two ways to participate in the defence of Helm's Dike. You can speak to Thenca for the Storied Tale, a story-focused experience. Or you can use the Epic Battles Panel for a more gameplay-intensive experience. To participate in the defence of Helm's Dike, open the Epic Battles Panel and select 'Helm's Dike' from the menu. After you successfully complete the defence, you will be returned to the location from which you entered it.\t\n2\tTalk to Gamling by the pile of straw near the western wall\tIt is after midnight at Helm's Deep. Gamling is by the pile of straw on the lower level of the fortress, by the western wall.\n3\tTalk to Gimli on the Deeping Wall\030Talk to Legolas on the Deeping Wall\tIt is after midnight at Helm's Deep. Gimli and Legolas are on the Deeping Wall. Gamling told you to take the eastern stairs up onto the wall in order to reach them.\n4\tTalk to Aragorn on the Deeping Wall\tIt is after midnight at Helm's Deep. Aragorn wishes to speak with you atop the Deeping Wall.\n",
[1973]="7000E062\n1\tGo with Yrjänä to meet your rival\tYrjänä is in the Great Lodge of Sûri-kylä. Yrjänä informed you that another has come claiming Narchuil and seeking the aid of the Lossoth in finding it.\n2\tTalk to Yrjänä\tYrjänä is in the Great Lodge of Sûri-kylä. You should speak with Yrjänä regarding Mordrambor's threats.\n",
[1974]="700379AC\n1\tTalk to Aragorn and help him inspire the defenders\tIt is after midnight at Helm's Deep. Aragorn is on the Deeping Wall, and wants your help preparing inspiring words for the beleaguered defenders. This is a Solo quest and cannot be completed with a Fellowship.\n2\tTalk to Aragorn on the Deeping Wall\tIt is after midnight at Helm's Deep. Aragorn is on the Deeping Wall, and wishes to speak with you now that you have done what you can to save the rapidly falling morale of the beleaguered defenders.\n",
[1975]="7000E063\n1\tTalk to Saija\tSaija is at Näky-kolo north west of Kuru-leiri. Yrjänä instructed you to seek the wisdom of Saija in order to find Narchuil.\n2\tSeek the body of the sea-monster in the Ice-bay of Forochel\tThe body of the sea-monster Saija spoke of lies in the Ice-bay of Forochel, east of Kuru-leiri. Saija directed you to seek Narchuil or news of it upon the body of a sea-monster which can be seen in the Ice-bay of Forochel.\n3\tTalk to Arvedui\tArvedui haunts the wreckage of a great Elf-ship frozen in the Ice-bay of Forochel. You have discovered the shade of Arvedui, the last king of Arthedain, haunting the wreckage of the Elf-ship which had come to rescue him so long ago. It may be that the shade will know the whereabouts of Narchuil.\n",
[1976]="700379AD\n1\tFind swordsmen and tell them to meet Aragorn at the postern gate (total: 4)\tIt is after midnight at Helm's Deep. Rohirric Swordsmen can be found in the open space between the Hornburg and the Deeping Wall. Aragorn has asked you to gather swordsmen to accompany him on a sortie beyond the wall.\n2\tTalk to Aragorn by the postern gate below the north-west tower\tIt is after midnight at Helm's Deep. Aragorn and Éomer are by the postern gate, below the north-west tower. You have given word to several swordsmen that Aragorn plans a sortie through the postern gate, and should see if that be enough.\n3\tTalk to Legolas atop the Deeping Wall\tIt is after midnight at Helm's Deep. Legolas is atop the Deeping Wall, accessible from ground-level by the eastern staircase. Aragorn has sent you to watch over the battle alongside Legolas.\n4\tIt is after midnight at Helm's Deep. There are two ways to participate in the defence of the Deeping Wall. You can speak to Thurketel for the Storied Tale, a story-focused experience. Or you can use the Epic Battles Panel for a more gameplay-intensive experience. To participate in the defence of the Deeping Wall, open the Epic Battles Panel and select 'The Deeping Wall' from the menu. After you successfully complete the defence, you will be returned to the location from which you entered it.\t\n5\tTalk to Éomer by the postern gate\tÉomer is below the north-west tower, by the postern gate. You have survived an attack on the Deeping Wall, and should see how Éomer and Aragorn fared in their sortie.\n",
[1977]="7000E064\n1\tFind the book of heraldry\tThe book of heraldry lies in the dwarf-mines where Arvedui and his people hid in Länsi-mâ. Arvedui instructed you to find the book of heraldry that was abandoned deep in the old dwarf-mines and bring it to a Ranger encamped in Forochel.\n2\tDeliver the book of heraldry to a Ranger encamped in Forochel\tThe Ranger is encamped at Sûri-kylä. Now that you have found the book of heraldry as directed by Arvedui, you should take it to the Ranger the ancient king spoke of.\n3\tTalk to Arvedui\tArevedui is in the wreckage of the Elf-ship, north along the Ice-bay in Talvi-mûri. Having delivered the book, you should return to Arvedui for further guidance.\n",
[1978]="700379EA\n1\tTalk to Gimli by the postern gate\tIt is after midnight at Helm's Deep. Gimli is by the postern gate, below the north-west tower.\n2\tTalk to Gléowine by the map table west of the Hornburg\tIt is after midnight at Helm's Deep. Gimli has asked you to check on Gléowine by the map table west of the Hornburg.\n3\tSet the tipped barrel near the western wall upright, and time will pass\tGléowine wants you to set the fallen barrel of weapons upright. Interacting with the tipped-over barrel near Gléowine will allow time to pass. Action will resume in the hours before dawn, with the next onslaught of the enemy.\n4\tTalk to Théoden outside the Hornburg\tIn the hours before dawn, the forces of Saruman press their advantage. Théoden King is outside the Hornburg.\n5\tIn the hours before dawn, the forces of Saruman press their advantage. There are two ways to participate in the defence of the Deeping-coomb. You can speak to Háma for the Storied Tale, a story-focused experience. Or you can use the Epic Battles Panel for a more gameplay-intensive experience. To participate in the defence of the Deep, open the Epic Battles Panel and select 'The Deeping-coomb' from the menu. After you successfully complete the defence, you will be returned to the location from which you entered it.\t\n6\tTalk to Aragorn on the second level, outside the Hornburg\tIn the hours before dawn, the forces of Saruman press their advantage. Aragorn is on the second level, outside the entrance to the Hornburg.\n7\tFind the breach in the Deeping Wall\030Defeat attacking uruks at the breach (total: 6)\030Talk to Sigferth by the breach\tIn the hours before dawn, the forces of Saruman press their advantage. Aragorn wants you to hurry to the breach in the Deeping Wall, east of the Hornburg, and help the survivors in the aftermath of the blast.\n8\tTalk to Aragorn on the second level, outside the Hornburg\tIn the hours before dawn, the forces of Saruman press their advantage. Aragorn is on the second level, outside the entrance to the Hornburg.\n",
[1979]="7000E065\n1\tTalk to Saija\tSaija is at Näky-kolo north west of Kuru-leiri. Arvedui told you that the captain of the Elf-ship did not perish with his vessel and suggested that you seek the knowledge of Saija regarding the fate of Aearil and his crew.\n",
[1980]="7000E066\n1\tSaija is at Näky-kolo north west of Kuru-leiri. Saija will tell you what you need to know, but wants you to perform two tasks for her.\t\n2\tTalk to Saija\tSaija is at Näky-kolo north west of Kuru-leiri. Now that you have completed both of the tasks she set before you, you should speak again with Saija.\n",
[1981]="7000E068\n1\tDefeat Ice-giants (total: 10)\tIce-giants can be found south and west of Näky-kolo. Saija has tasked you with defeating the Ice-giants that have come down from the mountains. She also suggests pulling them onto hot springs to weaken them.\n2\tTalk to Saija\tSaija is at Näky-kolo north west of Kuru-leiri. Having defeated the Ice-giants, you should return at once to Saija.\n",
[1982]="700379EC\n1\tFind Gimli in the Glittering Caves\tIn the hours before dawn, the forces of Saruman press their advantage. Aragorn has asked you to find Gimli in the Glittering Caves. The entrance to the caves is south of the Deeping Wall, where the stream runs out of the mountains.\n2\tTalk to Gimli in the Glittering Caves\tIn the hours before dawn, the forces of Saruman press their advantage. Gimli has been forced into the Glittering Caves during the fighting.\n3\tTalk to Gimli and secure the Glittering Caves\tIn the hours before dawn, the forces of Saruman press their advantage. Gimli is in the Glittering Caves, and wanted to speak with you about the next phase of the battle.\n4\tTalk to Gimli in the Glittering Caves\tIn the hours before dawn, the forces of Saruman press their advantage. Gimli is in the Glittering Caves, waiting to speak with you.\n",
[1983]="7000E067\n1\tDefeat ice-wights (total: 5)\tIce-wights can be found above Näky-kolo south and west from Näky-kolo. Saija has tasked you with banishing the ice-wights from the shores of Forochel.\n2\tTalk to Saija\tSaija is at Näky-kolo. Now that you have defeated many ice-wights, you should return to Saija as instructed.\n",
[1984]="700379ED\n1\tIn the hours before dawn, the forces of Saruman press their advantage. There are two ways to participate in the defence of the Glittering Caves. You can speak to Éomer for the Storied Tale, a story-focused experience. Or you can use the Epic Battles Panel for a more gameplay-intensive experience. To participate in the defence of the Glittering Caves, open the Epic Battles Panel and select 'Glittering Caves' from the menu. After you successfully complete the defence, you will be returned to the location from which you entered it.\t\n2\tTalk to Gimli in the Glittering Caves\tIn the hours before dawn, the forces of Saruman press their advantage. Gimli is in the Glittering Caves, and wishes to speak with you after pushing back the latest assault.\n3\tTalk to Aragorn outside the Hornburg\tIn the hours before dawn, the forces of Saruman press their advantage. Aragorn is on the second level, outside the Hornburg, and Gimli wants you to report to him of the dwarf's successes.\n",
})
